-- =============================================================================
-- 02_seed.sql — Demo database data
--
-- Run it AFTER 01_schema.sql and BEFORE 03_views.sql.
--
-- Literal INSERTs, keyed on `days_ago` (0 = today, 1 = yesterday). The table
-- stores no date: the date is born in the view, as current_date - days_ago.
-- Consequence: the data never ages. Run it today or a year from now and
-- "yesterday" is still yesterday — and the numbers are always the same.
--
-- Contents: 5 salespeople, 2,572 transactions across 180 days, 10 targets.
-- Check: total revenue R$ 17,966,842.11 · yesterday R$ 177,545.06 (+21.6%)
--        Bruno Tavares at 61% of target, on a 17.7% average discount.
--
-- WARNING: starts with a truncate — it wipes whatever is in the three tables.
--
-- This file was generated from 02_seed_generator.sql. The generator produces
-- the same data procedurally; this one freezes it as INSERTs, so that everyone
-- who runs it sees exactly the same numbers.
-- =============================================================================
set search_path = demo, public;
truncate table sales, targets, salespeople;

-- salespeople (5) — has to come first: the other two reference it

-- sales (2,572 transactions, 180 days)







-- targets — derived from each salesperson's own history
